      "html" : "<\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-163571\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-163571\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,serif;font-size:10pt;\">The storage volume of an on-site stormwater disposal system shall be measured 3 feet (610 mm) above the level of the water table. The location of the water table shall be verified at the time of the field investigation conducted in accordance with Section 1114.2. Unless otherwise approved by the New York City Department of Environmental Protection, the storage volume of the on-site stormwater disposal system shall accommodate the total stormwater volume calculated in this section. The stormwater volume shall be calculated as follows:<\/span><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-163572\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-163572\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,serif;font-size:10pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;1.&#160;&#160;&#160;Compute the runoff rate using Equations 11-1 and 11-2.<\/span><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-163573\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-163573\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,serif;font-size:10pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;2.&#160;&#160;&#160;Calculate the outflow rate due to infiltration, in cubic feet per second, using Equation 11-3.<\/span><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-163574\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-163574\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,serif;font-size:10pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;3.&#160;&#160;&#160;Calculate the outflow rate, in cubic feet per second per acre, of imperviousness using Equation 11-4.<\/span><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-163575\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-163575\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,serif;font-size:10pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;4.&#160;&#160;&#160;Calculate the duration of the design storm in minutes using Equation 11-5.<\/span><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-163576\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-163576\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,serif;font-size:10pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;5.&#160;&#160;&#160;Calculate the maximum required retention volume using Equation 11-6.<\/span><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-163577\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-163577\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: italic;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Q<\/span><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: italic;text-decoration:none;vertical-align: sub;display: inline;font-size:8pt;\">inf<\/span><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\"> = (<\/span><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: italic;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">FA<\/span><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: italic;text-decoration:none;vertical-align: sub;display: inline;font-size:8pt;\">min<\/span><span style